package Physics.Tests

use Libraries.Game.Layer3D
use Libraries.Interface.Item3D
use Libraries.Game.Physics.Vehicles.Vehicle

/*
Tests that a vehicle's engine speeds it up at the right rate, straight ahead.
After the test vehicle settles, each of its four wheels is given an engine
force of 1000. Together they push the 800 kilogram vehicle with 4000, so it
speeds up by 5 each second. After 2 seconds it should be moving at 10, which
is 36 kilometers per hour, and have gone 10. The wheels can grip with far
more than 1000 each, so they should not spin.

Which way a positive engine force drives depends on the vehicle, so the test
only checks how far it went, along its length, z.

The chassis is woken before driving, as VehicleMovementBehavior does, in
case it fell asleep while settling.
*/
class VehicleDriveTest is PhysicsWorldTest
    on create
        SetName("World: a vehicle's engine speeds it up")
    end

    action Run
        Layer3D layer = MakeWorld()
        AddGround(layer)
        Vehicle vehicle
        Item3D chassis = AddVehicle(layer, vehicle, 1.0)
        Advance(layer, 1.5)

        number startZ = chassis:GetZ()
        number startX = chassis:GetX()
        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < 4
            vehicle:SetEngineForce(1000, i)
            i = i + 1
        end
        chassis:Simulate(true)

        Advance(layer, 2)

        CheckNear("speed in kilometers per hour", vehicle:GetSpeedKilometersPerHour(), 36, 2)
        CheckNear("distance along z", Absolute(chassis:GetZ() - startZ), 10, 1)
        CheckAtMost("drift along x", Absolute(chassis:GetX() - startX), 0.1)
        CheckNear("chassis level", GetUp(chassis):GetY(), 1, 0.01)
    end
end
